"url":189,
"doc":"Class for performing operations for a specific Schedule. Attributes: class_object (object): Instance of Class Object. _commcell_object (object): Instance of the Commcell class. schedule_name (str): Name of the Schedule. schedule_id (int): Task ID of the Schedule. task_id (int): Task ID of the Schedule. _SCHEDULE (str): API service endpoint for the schedule. _MODIFYSCHEDULE (str): API service endpoint for modifying the schedule. _freq_type (dict): Dictionary mapping frequency types to their string representations. _week_of_month (dict): Dictionary mapping week numbers to their string representations. task_operation_type (dict): Dictionary mapping task operation types to their string representations. _criteria (dict): Criteria for the schedule. _pattern (dict): Pattern for the schedule. _task_options (dict): Task options for the schedule. _associations_json (dict): Associations JSON for the schedule. _description (str): Description of the schedule. _alert_type (str): Alert type for the schedule. _sub_task_option (dict): Subtask options for the schedule. _automatic_pattern (dict): Automatic pattern for the schedule. virtualServerRstOptions (dict): Virtual server restore options for the schedule. _schedule_disabled (bool): Indicates if the schedule is disabled. Usage: >>> schedule = Schedule(commcell_object, schedule_name='MySchedule') Initialise the Schedule class instance. Args: class_object (object): Instance of Class Object. schedule_name (str, optional): Name of the Schedule. Defaults to None. schedule_id (int, optional): Task ID of the Schedule. Defaults to None. task_id (int, optional): Task ID of the Schedule. Defaults to None. Raises: SDKException: If neither schedule_name nor schedule_id is provided. Usage: >>> schedule = Schedule(commcell_object, schedule_name='MySchedule') >>> schedule = Schedule(commcell_object, schedule_id=123)"
